  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Testing Laboratories (NAICS 541380) shows $398M in federal contract obligations for FY2026 to date. The sector recorded 2,958 awards with an average award size of $135K. Obligations fell 30.7% year over year. Fiscal-year obligations trended from $502M in FY21 to $575M in FY22, $619M in FY23, $671M in FY24, $574M in FY25, and $398M in FY26. The Department of Defense led buying activity with $182M in obligations, followed by the Department of Veterans Affairs with $46.7M and the Department of Health and Human Services with $34.1M. AGILE DEFENSE, LLC was the top vendor with $35M in obligations, followed by MERRICK & COMPANY with $28.8M and RAYTHEON COMPANY with $22.4M. These counts and dollar totals describe the market through the fiscal year to date and reflect contract obligations only, not full-year totals or other financial measures.",
